  "raw_label": "postponed_or_procedural",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Gurdwara Sri Guru Arjan Dev Ji (Regd.) vs Govt. Of Nct Of Delhi & Ors on 28 March, 2024 Author: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora Bench: Manmeet Pritam Singh Arora $~64 * IN THE HIGH COURT OF DELHI AT NEW DELHI + W.P.(C) 4573/2024 & CM APPL. 18763 GURDWARA SRI GURU ARJAN DEV JI (RE Through: Mr. Shivek Ra Ghai, Mr. Arp Saini and Mr. Advocates versus GOVT. OF NCT OF DELHI & ORS. Through: Mr. Anuj Ag GNCTD with Aakash Dahi Upadhyay, A Ms. Shilpa CORAM: HON'BLE THE ACTING CHIEF JUSTICE HON'BLE MS. JUSTICE MANMEET PRITAM SINGH ARORA % 28.03.2024 CM APPL. 18764/2024 (for exemption) Allowed, subject to all just exceptions.",
    "facts": "Present public interest petition has been filed seeking issuance of directions to quash the L-6 liquor license and other approvals granted by Respondent No. 1 (Govt. of NCT of Delhi) and Respondent No. 2 (DSCSC) to Respondent no. 4 (Mr. Rakesh Arora) for opening and operating liquor The authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. Learned counsel for the Petitioner states that on 13th March, 2024, the Petitioner through Respondent No. 4, came to know that Respondent no. 4 had applied and had been given approval for opening of L-6 license retail vend of Indian liquor/beer by Respondent Nos. 1 and 2 at subject premises on profit sharing basis/rent compensation basis. 4. He states that taking into consideration the illegal construction and encroachment upon public land by Respondent No. 4 at the proposed liquor vend, the Respondent No. 3 (MCD) issued a notice dated 18th March, 2024 to Respondent No. 4 with regard to illegal construction, encroachment and opening of the liquor shop at subject premises. He states that vide the aforementioned notice, Respondent no. 4 was requested to provide all related documents of the property such as sanctioned building plan/completion plan, regularization plan, ownership documents and charges deposited by him including copy of license/NOC's etc of the property within two days of receiving the above-mentioned letter. This is a digitally signed order. The authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. 7. He states that the approval for opening the proposed liquor vend has been obtained by the Respondent No. 4 in gross violation of the Delhi Excise Act, 2009, Rule 51 of Delhi Excise Rules, 2010 and the Master Plan of Delhi (MPD), 2021. Gurdwara Sri Guru Arjan Dev Ji (Regd.) vs Govt. Of Nct Of Delhi & Ors on 28 March, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/107017578/ 2",
    "arguments": ""
  },
